# ChatDSL Script: Generate Fake Sonnet and Run SVM Inference Classification
# Creates a fake sonnet in a composite Elizabethan style, saves it to 'fresh_dir',
# and runs classify_sonnet.py (MLX SVM) to predict if it is Real or Fake.

/run_unsafe

# Set fallback directory if not set by script runner
set fresh_dir = "/Users/jon2allen/projects/sonnets_svm/fresh_sonnets_testv2"

/model mistral_1
/temp 0.9
/multiline

Write a 14-line Shakespearean sonnet (ABAB CDCD EFEF GG in iambic pentameter).

STRICT STYLISTIC CONSTRAINTS:

Zero High-Frequency Clichés: Do NOT use the words rose, bloom, crimson, golden locks, silver threads, fleeting, sweet, fair, brow, or tread.

Obscure Metaphors: Use concrete, grounding early-modern imagery—legal terms (enfeoff, lease, audit), maritime navigation, heraldry, alchemy, or husbandry/agriculture.

Syntax & Enjambment: Avoid placing a complete thought on every line. Use heavy enjambment (run-on lines across stanzas), irregular caesuras (mid-line pauses), and inverted early-modern grammar rather than smooth modern sentence structures.


Lexical Variety: Maximize unique word count. Do not repeat content words across lines. Use early modern contractions naturally (o'er, ne'er, ta'en, th' earth).


;;

# 3. Save the generated fake sonnet to the fresh_dir directory
/save ${fresh_dir}/fake_sonnet_${seq}.txt

/echo Created fake sonnet at ${fresh_dir}/fake_sonnet_${seq}.txt:
/echo --------------------------------------------------
/file ${fresh_dir}/fake_sonnet_${seq}.txt
/showfile
/echo --------------------------------------------------

# 4. Run the MLX SVM classifier on the newly created fake sonnet and save analysis report
/echo Running MLX SVM Inference Classifier...
/run bash -c "/Users/jon2allen/projects/sonnets_svm/.venv/bin/python /Users/jon2allen/projects/sonnets_svm/classify_sonnet.py ${fresh_dir}/fake_sonnet_${seq}.txt --model_dir /Users/jon2allen/projects/sonnets_svm/sonnet_data_mlx "

/savevar RUN_COMPLETION ${fresh_dir}/fake_sonnet_${seq}_analysis.txt

# 5. Display the classifier output
/echo Classification Results:
/echo --------------------------------------------------
/echo ${RUN_COMPLETION}
/echo --------------------------------------------------


